  "findings": [
    "FSBL JTAG handoff invokes Xil_DCacheDisable before PM initialization/protection and JTAG exit. Later operations mean this call alone is not final live-state proof.",
    "AArch64 exit masks SCTLR_EL3 bits 0x1005 then takes WFE for no-handoff; exit UART marker precedes assembly exit, so marker alone does not prove terminal PC/state.",
    "Existing OCM startup initializes data/BSS before its EL3 control setup and subsequently enables EL3 C/I with 0x1006. It must not be treated as an uncached diagnostic entry.",
    "Existing cold OCM loader performs system reset and explicitly excludes DDR initialization. Reusing it after FSBL would discard the intended trained-state sequence.",
    "FSBL may remove PS/PL isolation when PL DONE is present; no-new-bitstream does not establish PL DDR-master quiescence."
  ],
  "next": "Implement a separate stackless EL3 entry observer and static OCM layout check; capture before control writes, no DDR loads/stores. Loader must verify FSBL terminal state before replacing overlapping OCM."
